WEBVTT

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.094
Welcome to Homlle chemical safety awareness.

00:00:03.314 --> 00:00:05.461
Before using a product, check that it

00:00:05.461 --> 00:00:07.609
is approved for the task and that

00:00:07.609 --> 00:00:09.756
you understand the instructions and task assessment.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:11.965
This short lesson does not qualify

00:00:11.965 --> 00:00:13.622
you to handle every chemical.

00:00:13.842 --> 00:00:17.079
If you are unsure, stop and ask a competent person.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.047
COSHH means Control of Substances Hazardous to Health.

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:24.604
In Great Britain, the 2002 regulations require

00:00:24.604 --> 00:00:27.942
risks from harmful substances to be controlled.

00:00:28.162 --> 00:00:31.979
Northern Ireland has separate 2003 regulations.

00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:36.527
These lessons support awareness; they are not an accredited qualification.

00:00:36.747 --> 00:00:39.515
Homlle must arrange competent, task-specific review

00:00:39.515 --> 00:00:42.282
before using them to authorise work.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.416
A hazard is something that can harm you.

00:00:45.636 --> 00:00:47.335
Risk depends on how you use

00:00:47.335 --> 00:00:48.750
it and who is exposed.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:52.132
Think about breathing in sprays, splashes onto skin

00:00:52.132 --> 00:00:54.899
or eyes, and contaminated hands near food.

00:00:55.119 --> 00:00:57.183
A beauty product or an everyday

00:00:57.183 --> 00:00:58.904
detergent can still cause harm.

00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:02.003
Consider the customer and anyone nearby too.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:05.552
The safety data sheet helps explain a product, but

00:01:05.552 --> 00:01:08.016
it is not the assessment of your job.

00:01:08.236 --> 00:01:10.797
Before work, find the approved method for

00:01:10.797 --> 00:01:13.359
the product, surface, room and people present.

00:01:13.579 --> 00:01:15.944
For example, a small bathroom may need a

00:01:15.944 --> 00:01:18.014
different method from an open work area.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:21.153
If the controls cannot be followed, pause and ask.

00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:24.080
First ask whether the hazardous substance

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.829
or process can be avoided.

00:01:26.049 --> 00:01:28.988
If not, use a safer approved alternative

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.927
and controls that reduce exposure, such as

00:01:31.927 --> 00:01:34.865
an appropriate dispensing method or effective extraction.

00:01:35.085 --> 00:01:37.928
Protective equipment is an extra layer, not

00:01:37.928 --> 00:01:40.364
permission to work with uncontrolled exposure.

00:01:40.584 --> 00:01:43.027
Never substitute products on your own.

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:46.781
Check the product name and label before each use.

00:01:47.001 --> 00:01:50.625
Keep the label readable and follow the manufacturer instructions.

00:01:50.845 --> 00:01:54.055
Never put a chemical into a food or drink container.

00:01:54.275 --> 00:01:57.207
An unlabelled bottle is not safe to guess with.

00:01:57.427 --> 00:02:00.828
Set it aside safely and ask for an approved replacement.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.305
Do not mix cleaning products, even if both seem familiar.

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:08.255
Mixing can create dangerous reactions.

00:02:08.475 --> 00:02:11.663
More concentrated does not mean safer or better.

00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:13.883
Follow the stated dilution and method

00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:15.550
for the product and surface.

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:18.705
If a customer asks for a different mixture, explain

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:21.315
that you must follow the safe approved method.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.117
Before starting, check ventilation, storage and the

00:02:25.117 --> 00:02:27.720
protective equipment specified for this task.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:30.519
Keep products away from children and pets.

00:02:30.739 --> 00:02:32.640
Gloves must be suitable for the

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.225
product and in good condition.

00:02:34.445 --> 00:02:38.401
If you notice skin irritation, breathing discomfort or another concern,

00:02:38.401 --> 00:02:42.357
stop exposure and report it through the agreed support route.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.941
PPE means personal protective equipment.

00:02:46.161 --> 00:02:49.961
The assessment decides whether chemical-resistant gloves, eye protection,

00:02:49.961 --> 00:02:53.286
protective clothing or other equipment is needed.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.970
Check the items fit you and work together.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.115
A glove material that suits one

00:02:58.115 --> 00:02:59.719
product may fail with another.

00:02:59.939 --> 00:03:02.638
Use the specified material and replacement instructions,

00:03:02.638 --> 00:03:04.951
not a guess based on colour.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:08.097
Check gloves for damage before use.

00:03:08.317 --> 00:03:10.994
Follow the trained removal method so the

00:03:10.994 --> 00:03:13.670
contaminated outside does not touch bare skin.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.845
Dispose of single-use gloves correctly; clean

00:03:16.845 --> 00:03:19.308
reusable equipment only as instructed.

00:03:19.528 --> 00:03:21.779
Wash and dry your hands afterwards.

00:03:21.999 --> 00:03:24.376
Gloves do not replace hand hygiene.

00:03:24.596 --> 00:03:26.371
Report red, itchy or cracked skin

00:03:26.371 --> 00:03:28.147
early and ask for a review.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.925
A basic face covering is not protection against chemical vapour.

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:37.141
Where a risk assessment requires respiratory protection, a competent person

00:03:37.141 --> 00:03:40.737
must select equipment suitable for the substance and wearer.

00:03:40.957 --> 00:03:43.442
Tight-fitting respirators need a face fit test and

00:03:43.442 --> 00:03:45.927
a fit check each time they are worn.

00:03:46.147 --> 00:03:48.552
Do not start a respirator-dependent task

00:03:48.552 --> 00:03:50.957
without the required training and equipment.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.506
For beauty work, assess the actual treatment.

00:03:54.726 --> 00:03:58.676
Nail dust, solvents and repeated wet work need suitable controls;

00:03:58.676 --> 00:04:02.231
hair products can also cause skin or breathing problems.

00:04:02.451 --> 00:04:06.374
Use product-specific instructions and any required extraction.

00:04:06.594 --> 00:04:09.914
This lesson does not qualify you to carry

00:04:09.914 --> 00:04:12.818
out a treatment or replace consultation, allergy

00:04:12.818 --> 00:04:15.723
precautions, infection control or practical beauty training.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.645
Keep lids closed and products secured so they cannot

00:04:19.645 --> 00:04:22.369
spill or be accessed by children or pets.

00:04:22.589 --> 00:04:26.279
Separate incompatible products according to their instructions.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:29.421
Do not decant into food or drink containers.

00:04:29.641 --> 00:04:34.183
Use the agreed disposal route for residues and contaminated materials.

00:04:34.403 --> 00:04:37.271
Do not pour an unfamiliar chemical down a drain.

00:04:37.491 --> 00:04:39.550
Ask if the route is unclear.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.369
For a spill or exposure, stop

00:04:42.369 --> 00:04:44.357
work and keep other people away.

00:04:44.577 --> 00:04:48.565
Follow the product emergency instructions and get appropriate help.

00:04:48.785 --> 00:04:51.651
Do not try to neutralise an unknown chemical

00:04:51.651 --> 00:04:54.159
or enter unsafe air to rescue equipment.

00:04:54.379 --> 00:04:58.397
In an immediate emergency, contact emergency services.

00:04:58.617 --> 00:05:00.753
Report the product and what happened.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.499
A customer hands you an unlabelled

00:05:03.499 --> 00:05:05.418
bottle and says it works well.

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:07.009
What should you do?

00:05:07.229 --> 00:05:09.362
Do not smell it to identify it, mix

00:05:09.362 --> 00:05:11.494
it or try it on a small patch.

00:05:11.714 --> 00:05:14.667
Explain that you need an approved labelled product.

00:05:14.887 --> 00:05:18.300
If none is available, pause the task and contact support.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.742
Next, complete the knowledge check in the guide.

00:05:21.962 --> 00:05:25.452
Before you work independently, a competent assessor should confirm

00:05:25.452 --> 00:05:28.554
that you can find the instructions, use the

00:05:28.554 --> 00:05:31.657
actual product safely and explain the emergency route.

00:05:31.877 --> 00:05:34.436
Record the lesson version and assessment.

00:05:34.656 --> 00:05:37.780
Watching this video alone does not approve you for work.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.821
Your assessor should check understanding, correct any

00:05:40.821 --> 00:05:43.641
gaps and observe the relevant practical skills.

00:05:43.861 --> 00:05:47.657
Do not treat video completion as automatic permission to work.
